From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dugs <dugahol@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:55:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Input: apple_z2: Advance past SEND_CALIBRATION in initial config

The initial-config scan skipped the SEND_CALIBRATION payload without
advancing fw_idx, so the next iteration parsed the payload as a command and
returned -EINVAL.  The device's real C1F5E,3 firmware was consequently
unusable and a synthetic C1F5E,4 container was required.  Advance over the
record like every other command.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c
@@ -4498,8 +4498,10 @@
 		size = get_unaligned_le32(fw->data + fw_idx);
 		fw_idx += sizeof(__le32);
 
-		if (load_cmd == LOAD_COMMAND_SEND_CALIBRATION)
+		if (load_cmd == LOAD_COMMAND_SEND_CALIBRATION) {
+			fw_idx = round_up(fw_idx + size, 4);
 			continue;
+		}
 		if (size > fw->size - fw_idx)
 			return -EINVAL;
 		if (load_cmd == LOAD_COMMAND_SEND_CALIBRATION_V2) {
